WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.233
MAN: [inaudible] .

00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:03.367
MAN: They're right here.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.533
They just went
in this building.

00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:05.767
Enemy just went
into this building.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:06.834
[inaudible].

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.400
CAPTAIN QUINCY BAHLER:
Sayidi, I need them

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.967
to say that nobody is in there.

00:00:16.967 --> 00:00:18.500
MAN: [inaudible].

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.233
CAPTAIN QUINCY BAHLER: Are
there friendly forces in here?

00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:21.734
No friendly.
MAN: [inaudible] .

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.200
CAPTAIN QUINCY BAHLER: OK,
that's all I'm asking, man.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.433
That's what I'm asking.

00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:27.600
NARRATOR: This is
what war looks like.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.433
When you're a captain
in the US Army.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:35.333
When you're less than 1,000
yards from the front lines.

00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.734
The last grid doesn't help me.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:39.100
I'm asking them to confirm
or deny if that's them.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.800
Sayidi, is this you?

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.066
Is this you?

00:00:43.066 --> 00:00:44.100
Is it Daesh or friendly?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.367
That's all I'm asking.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.066
NARRATOR: When you're working
alongside Iraqi generals.

00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:54.433
[inaudible].

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.900
CAPTAIN QUINCY BAHLER:
[inaudible] clear hot,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.867
approved.

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:02.734
General Ali.

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:04.233
NARRATOR: When making
the final calls

00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:06.266
that are the difference
between who lives--

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.233
Clear hot, clear hot.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.700
NARRATOR: And who dies.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.467
[applause]

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.333
CAPTAIN QUINCY BAHLER: They
have to seize the objective,

00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:16.834
so they still have
about 3 kilometers

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.000
to get to the Tigris.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.433
So this is one
victory for today,

00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:23.867
but there's weeks
of fighting left.

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:26.166
NARRATOR: Officially,
Bahler and the Americans

00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:28.734
are here only to
advise and assist.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.433
But the strikes
they're ordering will

00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:32.633
come from the American-led
coalition planes in the sky.

00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:33.934
CAPTAIN QUINCY
BAHLER: Sayidi, two

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:38.767
Daesh on a vroom right there.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:39.700
Yeah.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.500
[inaudible]

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.400
Are they reviewing the tape?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.333
Yeah, they did review.

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:43.533
It's a possible weapon.

00:01:46.266 --> 00:01:48.467
NARRATOR: Captain Bahler
does this all day,

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:52.133
trying to make sure what he
sees on his screens is right.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.500
Captain Bahler for
Captain Fitz, please.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.066
NARRATOR: That
ordering a strike will

00:01:55.066 --> 00:01:58.367
kill an ISIS fighter and not
an Iraqi soldier or civilian.

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.900
[inaudible] strike request.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.400
MAN: It's at strike, sir.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.934
[inaudible] [bleep].

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:07.000
Hey Dan, just for your SA,
we've got 200 dynamic on a moto.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.333
And we've got General Ali
here wanting us to strike it.

00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:11.367
I think it could go a
long way if we can get

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:14.367
these guys to approve rapidly.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.400
Yeah, they're traveling
straight towards friendlies.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.200
We've got to start
working the strike.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.633
Let's go.

